<TR>
<TD align=middle><IMG height=200 src="http://web.starmagazine.com/images/star/imported/8676.jpg" width=136 border=0></TD></TR>
<TR>
<TD align=middle><SPAN class=textsmbold>Madonna had a special concert!</SPAN></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE><FONT size=2>Being a friend of <B>Madonna</B>, as well as a fellow Kabbalist, has its perks. On May 21, The Spiritual Girl had a "Friends and Family" rehearsal of her Re- Invention tour at The Forum in Inglewood, Calif. A source says Kabbalah compatriots <B>Demi Moore</B>, <B>Ashton Kutcher</B> and <B>Barbra Streisand</B> were among the 300 select that also included <B>Camryn Manheim</B>, <B>Josh Groban</B> and his girlfriend, <B>January Jones</B>, who used to date Kutcher. But the real exclusive ticket was on May 23, <STRONG>a day before the tour</STRONG> kicked off. It was a show for just 50 friends -- "her Kabbalah family," says another source. Both Kutcher and Moore were there again and, at one point, says the second insider, <STRONG>Madonna "dedicated 'Crazy for You'to Rabbi Philip Berg and his wife Karen for their [wedding] anniversary."</STRONG> Mazel tov!</FONT></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE>
