<table border="0" cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFA8D3" width="100%"><tr><td align="left">
<font class="storytitle" color="#FFFFFF"><b><a href="modules.php?name=News&amp;file=categories&amp;op=newindex&amp;catid=7"><font class="storycat">Gossip</font></a>: Madonna Gives to the Troops?</b></font>
</td></tr></table></td></tr></table>

<table border="0" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="100%"><tr><td>
<a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=23"><img src="images/topics/look.gif" border="0" Alt="Look" align="right" hspace="10" vspace="10"></a>
<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><P><FONT face=Verdana></FONT></P>
<P><FONT style="FONT-SIZE: 16px; LINE-HEIGHT: 22px" color=#cc0000><B>Patriotic Postscript</B><BR></FONT>Before we get back to holiday mischief 'n' merriment--trust me, it gets more than a bit bitchy--I wanted to let you all know that Madonna's peeps are standing firm in their assertion that she <I>is not</I> positioning herself to perform for American troops in Iraq.</P>
<P>Which, bothered brother, is infuriating the Pentagon.</P>
<P>"Hours," snapped a source at the warmongering institution. "We spent <I>hours</I> on the phone with her representatives" discussing what the Big M. could do.</P>
<P>As reported <A style="COLOR: #cc0000" href="/Gossip/Awful/cauth/Archive2004/040527b.html" nocolor><FONT color=#cc0000>last week</FONT></A>, the Material Mama became less interested in a concert once her reps discovered the performance couldn't exactly be utilized for public consumption--so say Washington informants.</P>
<P>"You need better sources," barked Mad's flack.</P>
<P>How bitchy (it's why I live for Camp M., by the by). And I must point out something most interesting: I've observed a better track record (as far as not lying goes) with my Republican snoops. Wonder why?</P>
<P>CD P.S.: 500,000 Madonna discs were, somehow, donated to U.S. soldiers overseas. Wonder how that came about?</P>
<P><STRONG>Source: E!online, The Awful Truth</STRONG></P>
</font></div>
</td></tr></table>


</td></tr></table>


