<table border="0" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="100%"><tr><td>
<a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=23"><img src="images/topics/look.gif" border="0" Alt="Look" align="right" hspace="10" vspace="10"></a>
<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><SPAN class=norm12><STRONG>MADONNA</STRONG> looked a tad worse for wear as she left a posh LA restaurant on the arm of hubby <STRONG>GUY RITCHIE</STRONG>. 
<P>The superstar couple had been celebrating the start of Madge’s Re-Invention world tour with a glass (or several) of bubbly. 
<P>Guy, wearing a baseball cap and sporting a scruffy beard, did the protective bloke thing by guiding his missus out of the trendy Dolce restaurant and safely into their waiting car. 
<P>The couple were out with fellow Kabbalah devotees <STRONG>DEMI MOORE</STRONG> and <STRONG>ASHTON KUTCHER</STRONG> and various other pals from the Beverly Hills branch of the mystic church. <BR><BR>An onlooker said: “Madonna looked very happy when she left the restaurant. She was OK about walking out of the front door with Guy, knowing photographers were there. 
<P>“Demi and Ashton sneaked out the back because they didn’t want to be snapped.” 
<P>Madonna is on a gruelling tour, with 50 dates around the world. 
<P>She is thrilling sell-out crowds by mixing many of her old hits, including Vogue, Into The Groove and Holiday, in with newer material. 
<P>There’s no doubt she is still the Queen Of Pop. </P>
<P><STRONG>Source: The Sun.</STRONG></P></SPAN>
</font></div>
</td></tr></table>


</td></tr></table>


